After the v2.49.x cutover, hp1_agent comms became slow. Root cause:
asyncpg's prepared statement caches are incompatible with pgbouncer
transaction-pool mode. Each transaction may get a different backend
session; server-side prepared plans don't follow. Result: re-prepare
round trips per query at best, InvalidCachedStatementError at worst.

Fix: api/db/base.py detects DATABASE_URL pointing at the pgbouncer
socket (?host=/var/run/pgbouncer) and passes
  connect_args={'statement_cache_size': 0,
                'prepared_statement_cache_size': 0}
to create_async_engine. Direct-PG configurations are unchanged.

